WEBVTT

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.940
Senpai was there...

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:07.820
Right in the center of that battle.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:13.650
Hajime-senpai decided to use a certain 
power that was hidden within her.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:15.640
A certain power?

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:17.540
It's...

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.580
It'll be fine, Tsubasa-chan.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.800
We're not going to actually let Gel-chan die.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.210
What do you mean?

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:27.890
I'm going to borrow Katze-san's power.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.220
Thanks, Hajime-tan!

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.290
It's finally my time to shine!

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.140
Katze? Does she mean <i>that</i> Berg-Katze?

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.100
What's going on?

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.450
So that was what happened.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.570
<i>I'm sure that you're all 
aware, but Berg-Katze</i>

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:48.230
<i>is a violent being that had almost</i>

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.170
<i>led this country into destruction.</i>

00:00:48.230 --> 00:01:01.330
<b>Exclusive: Gatchaman Have an Important Announcement! 
 Misudachi Tsubasa Live in Studio!</b>

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.700
<i>Katze is currently inside 
Ichinose Hajime-senpai's body.</i>

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.250
<i>So what's Berg-Katze's power?</i>

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.330
<i>It is the power to completely 
become anyone else.</i>

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.740
<i>Hajime-senpai used that power 
to completely become Gelsadra.</i>

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.540
<i>Then the Gelsadra we saw was...</i>

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.090
<i>It was Hajime-senpai.</i>

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:15.290
What? You're kidding, right?

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.180
Then Gatchaman were beating the 
crap out of one of their own?

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:24.140
We argued for hours until this 
plan was finally carried out.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.860
What if you die because of that?!

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.670
I won't die.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.240
Using Katze's power is like 
making a pact with the devil!

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.080
Rui-kun, you were able to use the CROWDS,

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.360
and in the end, they became 
yours rather than Katze-san's.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.790
Well, that's... true, but...

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.750
I think the risk is too high.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.750
I find it hard to believe that by doing 
this, everyone will realize their mistake.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.900
Well, we won't know if we don't try!

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.070
Don't be ridiculous!

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:59.390
As your leader, I won't allow 
you to do something so reckless!

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:02.530
Then, Pai-Pai, what would you do as leader?

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:03.310
Huh?

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:08.680
Are you just going to watch as everyone 
just goes with the flow and kills Gel-chan?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.770
Or should we ask JJ?

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.610
Then we'll never be able to change.

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:20.100
But I can't attack you, Senpai!

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.720
Why's that?

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.830
Well... That's because you're not my enemy!

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.830
Then who is your enemy?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:28.830
That's...

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:33.040
Tsubasa-chan, you thought 
about this in Nagaoka, right?

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.250
Well, it's everyone.

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.220
Our enemy this time is all of us.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.260
Yup! That's why I'm also your enemy.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.970
I'll be fine even if you attack me.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:45.430
But...

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.960
It doesn't matter who's getting attacked,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:51.190
but I'm the only one who can do this.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.780
Whatchu talkin' bout, Hajime-tan?

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.180
This is all because of me.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.910
You're right, Katze-san.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.450
But I won't let you have your way, Katze-san.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.860
I'm the one that's going to get defeated!

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.540
And the ones that are going to defeat 
me are the people who I believe in!

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.460
I want to end this atmosphere with everyone!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:14.760
I think that Hajime-chan's exactly right.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.470
This is the ultimate chance 
for this planet to wake up

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.930
that will probably never come again.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.890
You said it, D-san!

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.760
I'm gloomy... But,

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.170
I won't let you die, no matter what!

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.900
Thanks, Utsutsu.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.850
This is the only way to 
save everyone. Got it?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.360
Then here we go!

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:43.660
Gatcha!

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.810
We're gonna kill Gel-chan!

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.960
We told you, didn't we, Tsubasa-chan?

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:56.220
Sometimes you have to risk your own life, 
in order to protect the things we hold dear.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.590
But I couldn't gather my resolve.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:10.020
I couldn't really tell if we 
needed to actually go that far.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:20.700
Tsubasa-chan, how did things come to this?

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.110
Because... We didn't 
actually think it through.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:29.760
We got caught up in the current, 
and this is where we ended up.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.770
We never even considered 
how alarming that was.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.400
I wonder why we didn't realize it.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.230
That's because our thoughts agreed 
with everyone else, so we felt safe.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.360
Then how did we come to the realization now?

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.550
Because we're alone.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.150
We were by ourselves, stopped, 
and took a moment to actually think.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.020
You're right. I thought about it, too.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.400
I wondered if everyone would really 
be satisfied if I disappeared.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:03.200
But then I realized that 
I didn't want to disappear.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.990
I want to stay here longer.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:07.360
I wanted to see you again, Tsubasa-chan.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:09.200
Gel-chan...

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.450
Hajime-chan told me that was okay.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.000
It made me happy.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.280
That's why I wanted to help Hajime-chan out.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:24.550
Hajime-chan said she wanted to ask 
everyone what to do with me again

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.180
after the atmosphere had calmed.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.220
I plan on following whatever 
the result may be.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.280
We were conflicted to the very end.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:41.320
Sugane, are you going to 
be able to defeat Hajime?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.780
I'm not sure, but we have to do this.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:48.610
She really doesn't falter, does she?

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.790
That's just who she is.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.450
That's exactly why

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.110
she won't die so easily.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.390
And then, that day came.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:09.260
What makes a hero?
What, what, what?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:15.530
What makes a hero?
What, what, what?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.510
Gel-chan.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.460
Hajime-chan. Thank you.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:28.110
This is nice. 
Everyone's become one rather nicely.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.250
All right, here we go!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.300
Go, Bird!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.000
All right, Katze-san. I'm counting on you.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.360
Okay! I haven't had kissy times in forever!

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.230
So excited!

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.540
Ge-lu-lu-lu-lu-lu...

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.630
Hurry it up, Katze-san!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.400
I see you're a demon, as usual.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:57.730
All right, here we go!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.790
And then we, the Gatchaman...

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:12.910
Tokyo Tachikawa

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:12.910
<b>Tense Battle: Gatchaman vs Gelsadra</b>

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:05.150
<i>One day has passed since the</i>

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.710
<i>decision was made that the Gatchaman 
would deal with Gelsadra.</i>

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:11.240
<i>It can truly be said that Tachikawa 
is in the calm before the st—</i>

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.910
<i>B-Behind you! Behind you!</i>

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:18.750
It's Gelsadra! 
Gelsadra has appeared in Tachikawa!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.090
All right! I'm going give this fight my all!

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:24.420
You guys need to come after me 
with everything you've got, too!

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.440
It'll be okay. We're all heroes!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.050
Digitize!

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:32.970
X-saucer!

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.140
That's not enough!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.990
Ow! Katze angry!

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.520
We've only just begun!

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.400
Burning Rain!

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:52.950
Just how foolish are we?

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.960
Burning Hammer!

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:01.930
Volcano!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.000
Gatcha! Gatcha!

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.440
Gatcha so annoying!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:21.870
They want a massacre!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.980
Don't you dare lose, Hajime!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.690
Take this!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.550
Up Down!

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:38.450
Creeping Cherry Blossoms!

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:47.040
They're serious... They're totally serious!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.340
More, everyone.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.760
More!

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.070
Rending Gale...

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.480
Blade!

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.860
I can't...

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:17.280
I can't keep up with you guys...

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.120
I'm not gonna lose...

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.330
I'm not gonna lose, no matter what!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:25.290
Phoenix Dive!

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:28.560
Come on, now...

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.460
At the time, the Kuu-samas 
finally started disappearing...

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.040
This is going too far...

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:35.480
...because everyone finally 
started to realize it.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:48.000
This was going too far. 
This atmosphere was too terrifying.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:51.730
Prepare yourself, you ugly monster.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.850
Go forth to your eternal slumber.

00:09:54.850 --> 00:09:56.620
Take this final blow!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.780
Please stop!

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.200
This is more than enough!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.330
You're in the way! Move!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.410
No!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.770
Tsubasa-chan, no.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.490
You can't be influenced 
by momentary feelings.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:10.630
Senpai...

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:15.320
You need to finalize your resolve,

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.340
to understand us.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:20.050
Everyone, can you hear me?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.710
Once you defeat me, 
we need to ask everyone again

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.100
what we should do with Gel-chan.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.500
I'm sure that everyone will think it through.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:34.050
I'm leaving the rest to you, Tsubasa-chan.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:36.320
Your words, Tsubasa-chan,

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.560
will reach everyone!

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:42.950
You're everyone's hero, Tsubasa-chan!

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:52.460
You're a hero, Tsubasa-chan!

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.880
The Infinite Blade, Storm!

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:11.690
That was the truth behind this plan.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:22.360
Heroes don't just save 
those in front of them.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:27.920
They must sometimes sacrifice 
themselves in order to save the many.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.250
That is what Senpai taught me.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.960
And where is Hajime-chan now?

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.690
Senpai has yet to regain consciousness.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.310
Hajime-chan...

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.780
Wait, she died?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.140
But it'll be okay.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.270
She will return.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.280
Because Senpai is the ultimate hero.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.990
We're now going to ask you all again...

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:04.750
What should happen to Gelsadra?

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.700
There are three choices.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.620
Leave him on Earth.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:11.330
Make him leave Earth.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.830
Leave it to Gatchaman.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.540
However,

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:19.000
this time, please don't reply 
as quickly as you usually do.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.370
We will tally the votes a month from now.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.800
Until then, you can change your 
answers as many times as you'd like.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:28.640
This is a very important issue 
that concerns all of us.

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:32.940
Please spend the next month 
thinking this over carefully,

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.390
and giving your own individual answer.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:38.000
I will be thinking, as well.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.160
Hang in there.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.330
Hang in there.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.370
Senpai, I kept my promise.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:55.210
Well done, Hajime.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:59.670
But take a look at this.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.730
<i>Poor Hajime-chan.</i>

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.070
<i>This is basically all 
Sadra's fault, isn't it?</i>

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:06.090
<i>GTFO, Grossadra!</i>

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.510
Everyone! There's a commotion outside!

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:13.850
<b>You Can Do It!! Hajime-chan!</b>

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:13.850
<b>Hajime-chan, fight!</b>

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.730
<b>Get out here, Sadra!
Apologize!</b>

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.730
Hajime-chan, thank you for the feels

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.900
Senpai wouldn't want any of this!

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.860
Sadra! Go Back to 
Your Planet Now!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:26.260
Everyone, is this what you really want?

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:28.840
Is this how you all really feel?

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.850
I was also scared to death

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:35.130
of being alone, and feeling 
different from everyone else...

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.210
But then I'll never be able to change!

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:41.600
I'm going to think on my own.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.560
That's why everyone needs 
to stand on their own feet,

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:48.680
and come up with their own answers.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.380
Please.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.790
We are thinking, Tsubasa-chan!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.500
Don't be so pushy.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.650
I mean, look at poor Hajime-chan.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.400
Sadra's unforgivable!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:01.650
This is how we really feel.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.140
No...

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.490
At this rate, nothing's going to change.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:13.450
<b>You can do it, Hajime-chan! 
 We're here for you! 
You guys are useless. lol
Wake up, Hajime-tan!
She totally deserves the People's Honor Award 
 She's a real hero (cry)
Actually, isn't that opinion causing an atmosphere?</b>

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:13.450
I can't help but feel like the atmosphere is 
starting to lean in another direction again.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:16.620
I agree, but it can't be helped.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.080
Why?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:21.560
They were suddenly shown 
Hajime in that state.

00:14:22.030 --> 00:14:24.920
It can't be helped that they'd 
all feel a certain way.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.830
But then they'll just make 
a foolish decision again!

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:31.360
Tsubasa-chan, calm down.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:35.370
<b>Jou-san's voice is so deep 
  Hajime-chan, fight! 
  Thanks for our peace! 
 Hajime so cute 
 Where the heck is Sadra? 
Let's really take the time to think for ourselves.
 Yeah, totally. Let's take our time.</b>

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:33.950
There's still time to vote.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.320
We're the ones that told everyone 
to take their time, remember?

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:39.350
<b>Yeah, totally. Let's take our time.
 Sugane has a good point 
Don't be swayed 
I'm gonna think to the end</b>

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.640
Yes, but...

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:43.510
But you know, everyone's saying 
how terrible Sadra is,

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:44.070
<b>Regarding
Sadra's Future</b>

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:44.070
<b>Leave Him On Earth
Make Him Leave Earth
Leave it to Gatchaman</b>

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.470
but he had some good qualities, too, didn't he?

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:49.520
Yeah. He was the first prime minister 
we all voted for, after all.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:52.960
He would always accept what we voted 
on our smart phones immediately.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.340
It was just for a moment, but don't you feel 
like you saw a glimpse of a good future?

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.420
Let's play once in a while!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:05.200
Yeah! Everyone's so serious lately.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.380
Sorry. I want to actually think about this.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:14.810
<b> But wouldn't it be scary if he stayed on Earth? 
 I know, right? 
 Let's think about this. 
Yeah, and not just have sympathy
I've been thinking too hard my head hurts lol 
It'd be easy if Sadra just left</b>

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:18.120
Senpai, everyone's thinking properly.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.640
Yuru-jii? I have a favor to ask.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.130
Wow, it's so pretty.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.330
You designed them, right, Tsubasa-chan?

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:43.030
Yes! In hopes that Hajime-senpai gets better!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:47.520
Can you see them, Hajime-chan?

00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:52.090
Hey! Say something, damn it! 
I'm going to bite you!

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:56.160
She sort of smiled just now!

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:58.770
Hang in there. Hang in there.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:02.980
Don't cry, Gel-chan.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:08.550
Let's smile! Look at how 
great the atmosphere is!

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.150
Right, Senpai?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:11.590
You...

00:16:11.590 --> 00:16:12.240
Huh?

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.820
...were sort of like Hajime just there.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:42.230
<b>Regarding Gelsadra's Future</b>

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:42.230
<b>Today is the Final Day to Vote.</b>

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:44.480
What should I do? I totally just voted.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.690
Me, too.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.400
Well, it should be fine. 
We all thought plenty about it.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:51.440
Right?

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.440
<i>I will now announce the results of the votes.</i>

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.710
<b>Regarding Gelsadra's Future
What Would You Like to Do With Gelsadra?</b>

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.200
We're counting on you, X.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:13.800
<b>Leave Him On Earth
Make Him Leave Earth
Leave it to Gatchaman</b>

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.130
The votes have been tallied.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.510
It's been decided!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.000
Gelsadra will remain on Earth.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:24.270
Everyone, thank you so much!

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.620
<b>Decided by Votes!! Gelsadra to Stay on Earth</b>

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:51.350
Senpai, you felt that, right?

00:17:51.350 --> 00:17:53.340
The atmosphere we're in right now.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:59.790
So, Gel-chan, what should we do now?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.470
And so, in this new direction of politics...

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.120
Hey, PM <i>Mulligan</i>.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.350
Akiyama
Toshio

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:26.350
Where'd you hide that dangerous alien?

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.150
What are you going to do if 
it causes an incident again?

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.830
Are you going to take responsibility?

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.810
You Gatchamanphile.

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:35.910
I'm not obsessed with anyone.

00:19:35.910 --> 00:19:39.070
I only followed through with 
what the people decided.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.400
Kishida 
Yasuyuki

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.410
Are you trying to blame this on the people?

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:48.350
Yes. This is the fault of me, Akiyama-san, 
Yoshikawa-san, Kishida-san...

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:51.080
This is all individually our faults.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:54.040
Now, then...

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:57.050
Relax, relax, relax, relax!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:58.600
Wrong.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:01.330
Aw, it's still wrong?

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:04.010
Don't get annoyed. One more time.

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:08.250
Relax, relax, relax, relax!

00:20:08.250 --> 00:20:08.970
Wrong.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:12.050
Aw, but why?!

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:15.770
Wh-What?

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:17.280
You want a piece of me?

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:20.080
Are you guys always stuck together like that?

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:21.990
It's more fun being separate.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.530
Here I go!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:35.580
Got it! Got it! Got it! got it!

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:39.840
Isn't this fun, Papa?

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.480
Yeah...

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:50.350
X, what do you think will happen to CROWDS?

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:52.510
Let's...

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.110
Take some time to think about that.

00:21:05.210 --> 00:21:08.730
Thank goodness. The Jou I know is back.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:12.620
Alan, I haven't changed at all.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.460
My dream will always be

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:19.090
world peace.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:24.770
Could you do something about 
this before world peace, though?

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.680
Sugane, we're moving out!

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:28.880
Right!

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:31.750
Hajime!

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:35.720
She moved!

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.850
I slept so well.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:55.960
Katze-san has descended! 
Good morning, stupid shitty bitch planet!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:57.330
Hajime-chan.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:58.930
I'm gloomy!

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.500
Hajime!

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.490
Welcome back, Hajime-chan!

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:05.010
Senpai!

00:22:06.120 --> 00:22:08.750
I can't breathe, Tsubasa-chan.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:11.570
What happened after that?

00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:15.020
Um... A lot's happened since then.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:18.100
Um... I wonder where I should start...

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.940
Um, uh...

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:25.490
You haven't changed at all, Tsubasa-chan.

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:27.960
That's not true!

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:30.570
I've grown quite a bit!

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:35.080
Then you can take your time 
and tell me all about it.

00:22:35.380 --> 00:22:36.630
Roger!

00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:40.140
All right, everyone! Ready, and...

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:41.210
Gatcha!

00:22:41.520 --> 00:22:42.710
Gatcha!

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>The End</b>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.010
The end.
